Description: Give a window a target monitor, which restoring sets from the stored state, as mutter 50.2 does.
 Mutter 50.1 restores a maximized, tiled or fullscreen window by moving it to its stored rectangle and then
 maximizing, tiling or making it fullscreen, and the constraints fall back to the monitor the window was created on
 when a move or resize has no valid rectangle. Mutter 50.2 gives a window a target monitor, the monitor window
 management operations act on, which restoring sets from the stored rectangle and the constraints fall back to.
 restore-maximized-client-monitor.patch builds on it for a window GTK maximizes before restoring it.
 .
 This is upstream's merge request 4960 for issue 4158, without its test of resized tiled windows, which needs test
 helpers 50.1 does not have: 5d6d76bb, 645bd87a, 6bee1e5b, a475ba48, 6aaeacc6, 8e273315, 27870756, 17d85057,
 d0633d77 and 5338fbb2, with the stacking tests added to the list in src/tests/meson.build by hand. It also has
 371973f3, which fixes a crash after a display reconfiguration with a window whose target monitor was removed, issue
 4891, and which is 07461c96 of mutter 50.3.
Origin: upstream, https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/mutter/-/merge_requests/4960
Bug: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/mutter/-/issues/4158
Applied-Upstream: 50.3
Last-Update: 2026-11-16
